type: api
title: Vault KV read
description: |-
  Reads a secret over plain HTTP the same way you would call Vault or OpenBao
  KV v2 (`GET /v1/secret/data/...` + `X-Vault-Token`).

  `setenv` promotes `token` into the runtime environment so later APIs can use
  `e:api_token` / `<<e:api_token>>`.

  Default URL hits the local mock in this example. Point `vault_addr` at a real
  Vault/OpenBao and set `vault_token` to use your cluster instead.
protocol: http
method: get
url: <<e:vault_addr>>/v1/secret/data/<<e:vault_secret_path>>
headers:
  X-Vault-Token: <<e:vault_token>>
  Accept: application/json
format: json
outputs:
  api_token: body.data.data.token
setenv:
  api_token: body.data.data.token
